<p>This feels pretty reminiscent of something like <a href="/scp-993">SCP-993</a> or <a href="/scp-2030">SCP-2030</a> without really doing anything hugely new with the concept. It also feels like it relies really heavily on shock horror, particularly that of massive child death, and I would really urge you to not do that.</p>
<p>Beyond this: your actual pitch is too heavily summarised, which makes it really hard to tell how all the stuff fits together. E.g., you mention the 'children's show and candy are mysteriously causing disappearances' but there's not really any indication of how this works: is it like, people on the show disappear? People who watch it? How does the candy tie in?</p>
<p>There's talk of an exploration log in the middle of the central narrative which seems fine; but you mention that 'Addendums and follow up memos follow to round out the story' but I don't really have a feel for either a) what the core of the story is or b) how they round out the story; and I'm left feeling&#8230;not very enthused by any part of this.</p>

