<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So this is like&#8230;clearly a narrative focussed around the recovery log and the exploration log; but I only really have a broad strokes view of what happens in both, and neither seems&#8230;hugely interesting to me to read? My concern is that it sounds like both are just going to end up being very matter of fact things that don't really add much narratively to this; and I'd really like to know a little more about your plans around them before I'd be willing to even consider greenlighting this.</p>
<p>My, other concern is that the SCP feels&#8230;a little too x-man-y and complex to me: it has a range of anomalous powers that are kinda thematically linked but it feels a bit lacking in cohesion: elements like the pocket dimension, and the 'extend all organs and bones' part feel sort of tacked on in an effort to make this more interesting and my concern is that you've kinda mistaken 'can do lots of cool things' for 'interesting idea to read about'.</p>
<p>I guess really what I want to know is how you're really wanting to convey a sense of horror to a reader here: the very short summary of both the recovery mission and the exploration log makes it feel like they were both kinda carried out with minimal effort and danger, and that feels very unconducive to a good horror atmosphere, y'know?</p>
<p>I'm also not convinced that a lengthy section on how the Foundation got this into containment will feel that satisfying to read: it kinda feels like the sort of thing were the ConProcs would give away that it's in Containment, and so the rest of the article is just&#8230;moving pieces into the position we already know it's in? It feels to me that focussing on what happens once it's contained might be more interesting; though it feels like this is the kinda SCP that might force that into a generic containment breach story and I would strongly urge you to try and find a different angle to that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

